  "body": "## Problem\n\nNo `node --test` run had a timeout, so a test that never settled hung its CI job until `timeout-minutes` (up to 10 min) or hung `npm run fast` forever, with no test name. Tests also asserted on wall-clock deltas (`Date.now() - started < 2000`, `performance.now()` medians) and set ad-hoc per-test timeouts (claim-lock 180 s for a 4 s test): the load-flaky class the tracker kept fixing one instance at a time.\n\n## Change\n\n- `scripts/lib/test-timeout.ts` owns one ceiling: `--test-timeout=60000` plus `--test-force-exit` (a timed-out test's live handle cannot keep its file running). `scripts/test-suite.mjs` (npm test, CI shards) and `scripts/fast-check.ts` (`testRunnerArgs`) both use it; `KRN_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS` lowers it for the runners' own tests.\n- `test/test-timeout.test.ts` runs a never-settling fixture through both runners at a 1 s ceiling: it fails by name (`not ok - never settles`, `test timed out after 1000ms`) and the next test still runs.\n- `test/rules/test-hygiene.test.mjs` bans wall-clock deltas (`Date.now()/performance.now() - x`, `process.hrtime`) and per-test `timeout` options, with a per-file allowlist and reason; a seeded fixture set proves it reports exactly the 6 seeded violations and none of 6 clean shapes (deadline polls, `spawnSync` timeouts, computed timestamps).\n- Violations removed: per-test timeouts in claim-lock (6), codex-cancel, systemd-scope-collect, codex-replay; elapsed-time assertions rewritten as conditions: codex-stale-scope (bounded `waitFor` deadline), setup-marker (ready once the holder PID is gone), operator-inbox (every run finishes inside the hook's configured 5 s timeout), context-restart (`spawnSync` timeout). codex-registration and codex-usage keep their sized timeouts (120 s condition waits) on the allowlist.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test test/test-timeout.test.ts`: pass 3, fail 0.\n- `npm run fast`: PASS (14 changed, 27 tests).\n- `npm test`: exit 0, 981 tests, 0 failed.\n\n## Task\n\nTicket: t-6np1gz9 (closed in this PR). Retro: a child `node --test` spawned from a test inherits `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` and silently skips its files, so the ceiling test strips it; an argv builder must take the child's env, not read the caller's. Roadmap: unchanged (t-6np1gz9 had no row).\n\nAgent: Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
